<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM4-STALE-SPRINT-DOC-TLS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM4-STALE-SPRINT-DOC-TLS" ;
  triage:title "sprint-AM4-delete-legacy-peer.md still requires an AL.7 TLS/mTLS adapter that was never implemented and is not a real AM.4 requirement" ;
  triage:description "docs/plans/phase-am/sprint-AM4-delete-legacy-peer.md deliverable 2 requires 'Retain only AL.7's TLS physical adapter around the shared AL.4 client and AL.2 handler', and its acceptance criteria / required validation list 'TLS/trust negative cases still fail before application dispatch' and 'M5 clean-checkout direct-send and mTLS-negative proof'. No TLS/mTLS implementation exists anywhere in crates/atm-http-runtime (confirmed by grep -- client.rs uses plain reqwest/TCP only). docs/plans/phase-am/plan-phase-am.md's AM.4 section was already corrected to state 'AL.7's TLS adapter was never implemented and TLS is quarantined outside the MVP, so it is neither a retained dependency nor an AM.4 proof requirement', and the AM.1 ledger's own critical-review item AM-PLAN-002 is checked off as resolving exactly this premise -- but the standalone sprint doc's literal text was never updated to match. Independently found by req-qa (as a Blocking cross-doc-conflict finding, ATM-QA-001) and arch-qa (as an Important gate-artifact finding, ARCH-003); both converged on the identical root cause and remediation. Quality-mgr confirms the contradiction is real via direct read of both files, but downgrades req-qa's Blocking classification to Important: the actual authoritative doc per this dispatch (plan-phase-am.md) is already correct, the code is correctly scoped against it, and this is pure documentation staleness with zero functional/security impact -- not a defect in the shipped behavior." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "doc-gap" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-10T21:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AM-S4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-10T21:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AM4-STALE-SPRINT-DOC-TLS/AM4-QA1-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

